---

## 1. Core Velox Format-Level Readers (4 total)

These are registered via `registerReaderFactory()` in the `velox/dwio/` layer:

| # | Format | Factory Class | Reader Class | Path |
|---|--------|---------------|-------------|------|
| 1 | **DWRF** | `DwrfReaderFactory` | `DwrfReader` | `velox/dwio/dwrf/reader/DwrfReader.h` |
| 2 | **ORC** | `OrcReaderFactory` | `DwrfReader` (delegates) | `velox/dwio/orc/reader/OrcReader.h` |
| 3 | **Parquet** | `ParquetReaderFactory` | `ParquetReader` | `velox/dwio/parquet/reader/ParquetReader.h` |
| 4 | **Text** | `TextReaderFactory` | `TextReader` | `velox/dwio/text/reader/TextReader.h` |

Note: ORC has its own factory but internally calls `DwrfReader::create()` -- no separate ORC reader implementation.

## 2. Core Velox Format-Level Writers (3 total)

Registered via `registerWriterFactory()`:

| # | Format | Factory Class | Writer Class | Path |
|---|--------|---------------|-------------|------|
| 1 | **DWRF** | `DwrfWriterFactory` | `dwrf::Writer` | `velox/dwio/dwrf/writer/Writer.h` |
| 2 | **Parquet** | `ParquetWriterFactory` | `parquet::Writer` | `velox/dwio/parquet/writer/Writer.h` |
| 3 | **Text** | `TextWriterFactory` | `TextWriter` | `velox/dwio/text/writer/TextWriter.h` |

Note: **No ORC writer** exists in Velox. ORC files can be *read* (via DWRF reader delegation), but not written as ORC format.

## 3. Core Connector DataSources / DataSinks

**DataSources (6 total):**

| # | Connector | Class | Inherits | File Formats | Type |
|---|-----------|-------|----------|-------------|------|
| 1 | Hive | `HiveDataSource` | `DataSource` | DWRF, ORC, Parquet, Text | File I/O |
| 2 | Iceberg | `IcebergDataSource` | `HiveDataSource` | DWRF, ORC, Parquet | File I/O |
| 3 | Paimon | `PaimonDataSource` | `HiveDataSource` | ORC, Parquet | File I/O |
| 4 | TPCH | `TpchDataSource` | `DataSource` | Generated | Synthetic |
| 5 | TPC-DS | `TpcdsDataSource` | `DataSource` | Generated | Synthetic |
| 6 | Fuzzer | `FuzzerDataSource` | `DataSource` | Synthetic | Synthetic |

**DataSinks (2 total):**

| # | Connector | Class | Inherits | File Formats |
|---|-----------|-------|----------|-------------|
| 1 | Hive | `HiveDataSink` | `DataSink` | DWRF, Parquet, Text |
| 2 | Iceberg | `IcebergDataSink` | `HiveDataSink` | DWRF, Parquet |

## 4. cuDF Experimental Readers/Writers (under `velox/experimental/cudf/`)

| # | Type | cuDF Class | Inherits | Format | libcudf Backend | Core Counterpart | Status |
|---|------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------------|-----------------|--------|
| 1 | **Reader** | `CudfHiveDataSource` | `DataSource` | Parquet only | `cudf::io::chunked_parquet_reader` + optional `hybrid_scan_reader` | `HiveDataSource` | Active |
| 2 | **Writer** | `CudfHiveDataSink` | `DataSink` | Parquet only | `cudf::io::chunked_parquet_writer` | `HiveDataSink` | Exists, **NOT wired** into connector |

Key details:
- `CudfHiveConnector` (line 54 in `CudfHiveConnector.h`) has `// TODO (dm): Re-add data sink` -- `createDataSink()` is not overridden
- The write test `velox_cudf_table_write_test` is commented out in CMakeLists.txt
- cuDF bypasses Velox's `dwio` layer entirely -- it uses libcudf's native Parquet I/O

## 5. Coverage Matrix: Format x Layer

| Format | Core Reader | Core Writer | cuDF Reader | cuDF Writer | cuDF Read % | cuDF Write % |
|--------|:-----------:|:-----------:|:-----------:|:-----------:|:-----------:|:------------:|
| **DWRF** | DwrfReader | dwrf::Writer | -- | -- | 0% | 0% |
| **ORC** | OrcReader (via DWRF) | None | -- | N/A | 0% | N/A |
| **Parquet** | ParquetReader | parquet::Writer | CudfHiveDataSource | CudfHiveDataSink | **100%** | **~50%** (not wired) |
| **Text** | TextReader | TextWriter | -- | -- | 0% | 0% |

## 6. Connector-Level Coverage

| Connector | Core Source | Core Sink | cuDF Source | cuDF Sink | Notes |
|-----------|:----------:|:---------:|:-----------:|:---------:|-------|
| **Hive** | HiveDataSource | HiveDataSink | **CudfHiveDataSource** | CudfHiveDataSink (not wired) | Only Parquet covered on GPU |
| **Iceberg** | IcebergDataSource | IcebergDataSink | -- | -- | No cuDF coverage |
| **Paimon** | PaimonDataSource | None | -- | N/A | No cuDF coverage |
| **TPCH** | TpchDataSource | None | N/A | N/A | Generated data |
| **TPC-DS** | TpcdsDataSource | None | N/A | N/A | Generated data |
| **Fuzzer** | FuzzerDataSource | None | N/A | N/A | Synthetic data |

---

## Key Takeaways

1. **cuDF covers only 1 of 4 file formats** (Parquet) for reading, and that same 1 format partially for writing
2. **cuDF covers only 1 of 3 file-format connectors** (Hive) -- Iceberg and Paimon have no GPU path
3. The cuDF writer (`CudfHiveDataSink`) exists as a class but is **not connected** to `CudfHiveConnector` yet (TODO in source)
4. cuDF bypasses the Velox `dwio` layer entirely, using `libcudf`'s native Parquet I/O instead
5. DWRF, ORC, and Text formats have **zero** GPU coverage

I also saved a styled HTML version of all these tables at `/home/knataraj/AGENT/velox-reader-writer-coverage-matrix.html` that you can open in a browser.
